<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93282" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάπων</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ</span>,
		Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sapo, soap</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ Γερμανικῷ σμήγματι </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλεῖται δὲ ς</span>.) <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.29.59
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.586
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CD</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>:—a Gallic invention (hair-dye) adopted by the
			Germans acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				28.191
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span>,
				Seren.Sammon.<i><span class="en">
				153
			</span></i>.] (The Germanic forms (OHG. <i>seifa</i>, O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>sápe</i>, etc.) come fr.prim. Germanic
				<i>*saipjō</i>, whence also Finn. <i>saippio</i>;
			cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σήπων</span>.)</div>
